From: richie-rich90454 <rjiang880@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0008/0014] Point the marketplace at Open VSX

This patch changes product.json extensionsGallery to Open VSX.

Rationale: the Microsoft marketplace is proprietary Terms of Service.
Open VSX serves every extension we need.

Touches:
  - product.json (extensionsGallery)

Target extensionsGallery:
  {
    "serviceUrl": "https://open-vsx.org/vscode/gallery",
    "itemUrl": "https://open-vsx.org/vscode/item",
    "resourceUrlTemplate": "https://open-vsx.org/vscode/asset/{publisher}/{name}/{version}/Microsoft.VisualStudio.Code.WebResources/extension",
    "extensionUrlTemplate": "https://open-vsx.org/vscode/asset/{publisher}/{name}/{version}/Microsoft.VisualStudio.Code.WebResources/extension"
  }

Consequences: Microsoft-only extensions (C#, Live Share, Copilot Chat,
Remote-*) are unavailable. The gallery URL is a policy field, so an
enterprise mirror needs no rebuild.

Diff: authored on the upstream checkout (see build.sh).
Verification: install-from-Open-VSX smoke test.
